+//   stored pixels takes the edge value, the byte of the top-left stored pixel's color. A mask becomes a second plane
+//   (opaque: the white byte times alpha; transparent and outside: the black byte).
+// - Each pass is a horizontal then a vertical running box sum over 2r + 1 bytes, divided with truncation; positions
+//   outside the row count as the edge value (also for the mask plane).
+// - The planes are dithered into the result: the ordered types keep a pixel where the byte exceeds the type's table
+//   value at (x + xPhase, y + yPhase) (the drawFaded tables); None keeps bytes at or above xPhase (128 when 0); the
+//   error diffusion types use their own byte arithmetic, which wraps.
