+// - each C pointer has at most one userdata: pushing a pointer that already has a live userdata pushes that same
+//   userdata (and gives no handle when its class differs from the one asked for);
+// - a LuaUDObject handle stays valid for as long as its userdata lives, so C code can keep it between calls;
+// - user values read back as nil in the Simulator, whatever was set; setUserValue leaves the value and pushes
+//   the object, getUserValue pushes nil.
