+// The C API JSON decoder (JsonDecoder.cpp) behaves as on the device (3.1.2): the same byte stream
+// state machine, number parsing, error messages and line numbers, paths (including the reversed array index digits),
+// skipping, returnString mode and callback order. The game's callbacks receive an emulated working copy of its
+// json_decoder, which is written before and read back after every callback, so changes a callback makes (another
+// callback, userdata, returnString) apply from then on, and are restored when a sublist ends. The reader
+// is called on demand with a 1024-byte buffer, as on the device.
+namespace {
